Why Is Demand Increasing?
Faster identity verification: Police departments and investigative agencies are adopting fingerprint, facial, and iris-recognition systems to accelerate identification and support investigative workflows.
Modernization of public-safety infrastructure: Digital evidence systems, connected field devices, and integrated databases help agencies coordinate information and manage growing volumes of biometric records.
Multimodal biometric technology: Combining multiple biometric characteristics can strengthen identity verification and reduce dependence on a single identification method, although performance depends on system quality and operating conditions.

Law Enforcement Biometrics Watch: Edge AI and Responsible Data Use
Biometric platforms are increasingly incorporating AI-based matching, mobile capture, and cloud-connected analytics. Edge processing can support faster field identification while reducing the need to transfer all data to centralized systems. At the same time, agencies must consider data protection, accuracy, auditability, and the risk of false matches. Procurement decisions increasingly depend on both technical performance and the ability to meet applicable legal and oversight requirements.

