Why This Market Matters
Biometric technologies can help law enforcement agencies identify individuals, organize forensic evidence, and improve investigative efficiency. However, deployment requires robust safeguards for sensitive personal data, documented system performance, appropriate human review, and compliance with applicable laws. Budget constraints, interoperability challenges, and public concerns about surveillance can influence purchasing decisions and deployment timelines.

